// EXPECT-ERROR: an initialiser here would run once at load
// Arrays take the same rule rather than an exception, which is the whole reason
// the rule is shaped this way: with no `rep movsb` in the 8086 subset there is
// no cheap way to re-initialise an array, so load-time is the only thing an
// array initialiser could ever be.
//
// One consequence: a nested array must be sized, since `u8[] buf` on its own is
// already an error for having neither a size nor an initialiser.
sub f {
  u8[3] buf = [ 1, 2, 3 ]
  _al = buf[0]
}
f()
